{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386677-what-do-magi-understand-about-technocrats","id":1386677,"title":"What do Magi understand about Technocrats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T06:57:36-07:00","id":1386677,"title":"What do Magi understand about Technocrats?","content":"Feel free to share your wider opinions, but I am specifically concerned with this question: Does your typical mage know that a typical technocrat is full of shit? Meaning, does the mage recognize that the technocrat is doing true magick, or is the mage oblivious to this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T07:21:20-07:00","id":1386682,"title":"","content":"In my games, a typical Technocrat <i>isn't</i> full of shit \u2014 meaning, it's entirely possible that the Union is right in its assertion that Enlightened Science and Awakened Magick are two different things. Though if they are, they're closely related things. <br /> <br /> That said, in my games, the Traditions <i>claim</i> that the Technocrat is doing True Magick; and <i>they</i> may be right. Not that that changes anything about the Technocracy's capabilities or operations. <br /> <br /> But ultimately, it's the Disparates who have the real inside track: their view in general is that the Technocracy and Traditions are having a huge dick-waving contest (called the Ascension War) over fine points of philosophy that generally don't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T09:03:02-07:00","id":1386709,"title":"","content":"In games I run, most Tradition Mages &quot;know&quot; it because the older mages tell them, but the younger mages, aside from virtual adepts and etherites, usually don't get it's significance and sometimes don't believe it until they run into primium shielding or find a tradition mage using countermagick or unweaving against technocratic effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:11:05-07:00","id":1386822,"title":"","content":"It really depends on the level of education of the individual magi but ultimately the youngest of them will know that Technocrats are full of shit the same way that they know that everything else is full of shit... they're the ones who have The Truth and everyone else is deluding themselves to some degree.<br /> <br /> The closest to understanding the Technocrats and their practices are the Society of Ether and Virtual Adepts and both of these traditions have specific issues with the limits and reductionism of the technocratic paradigm, while the average traditionalist simply disdains the technocrats as a whole.<br /> <br /> The technomancers specifically disdain the technocrats with their limited vision of technologies potential and the masses capacity to excel with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}